<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions for tiny-ledger (issue #11, spec §12.1 stage 11).

  THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY. It exists so that the first suppression anyone needs has an
  obvious, reviewed home instead of being added as a `-D` flag on a CI line, where nobody would
  ever read it again.

  THE RULE, and it is the same one ci.yml already applies to the Keycloak realm file:

    1. Every <suppress> names a SPECIFIC <cve> (or a specific <vulnerabilityName>), and carries a
       <notes> saying why that CVE does not apply to THIS project — the code path that is not
       reached, the feature that is not enabled, the transitive dependency that is test-scope only.
       "False positive" alone is not a reason; it is a claim awaiting one.

    2. A BLANKET SUPPRESSION IS NEVER ACCEPTABLE. No bare <packageUrl> or <filePath> element
       without a CVE beside it, and no regex broad enough to cover a vulnerability nobody has seen
       yet. A standing exemption silently covers future content — which is exactly the reasoning
       ci.yml gives for refusing to allowlist docker/keycloak/realm-tiny-ledger.json by path: there
       is no active finding to suppress, and a path exemption would also cover a real secret pasted
       into that file by mistake tomorrow.

    3. Prefer fixing to suppressing. A suppression with an <until> date is better than one without,
       because it fails again rather than becoming permanent by neglect.

  Shape of an acceptable entry, for whoever adds the first one:

    <suppress until="2027-01-01Z">
      <notes>CVE-2000-0000 is in the XYZ parser, reached only via the servlet filter this project
             does not register. Verified by ... . Re-check when abc is upgraded past 1.2.3.</notes>
      <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.example/abc@.*$</packageUrl>
      <cve>CVE-2000-0000</cve>
    </suppress>

  Note that an empty ruleset is NOT inert with respect to the gate: pom.xml sets
  failBuildOnCVSS to 7, so with nothing suppressed here every CVSS>=7.0 finding fails the build.
  That is the intended starting position.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
</suppressions>
